                "senderName": "NWS Tallahassee FL",
                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 8 at 2:38AM EDT until October 10 at 8:00PM EDT by NWS Tallahassee FL",
                "description": "* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of southeast Alabama, the Florida Panhandle and\nBig Bend, and southwest Georgia.\n\n* WHEN...From Friday afternoon through Saturday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Hurricane Isaias is expected to bring bands of heavy rainfall to\nthe area. Widespread totals of 3 to 7 inches are expected with\nlocalized amounts of 10 inches. Given saturated soils from recent\nheavy rainfall, flash flooding is expected. Considerable flash\nflooding is possible where bands of heavy rain move repeatedly\nover the same area.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be alert for possible Flood\nWarnings. Those living in areas prone to flooding should be prepared\nto take action should flooding develop.",
                "response": "Prepare",
                "note": null,
