                "headline": "Flood Watch issued October 7 at 3:07PM HST until October 8 at 6:00PM HST by NWS Honolulu HI",
                "description": "A deepening area of low pressure north of the Hawaiian Islands will\ndraw deep tropical moisture northward, resulting in a threat for\nheavy rain over Kauai and Oahu tonight through Thursday.\n\n* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues to be\npossible.\n\n* WHERE...Oahu, Kauai, and Niihau.\n\n* WHEN...Through Thursday afternoon.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flood prone roads and other low lying areas may be closed\ndue to elevated runoff and overflowing streams. Urban areas may\nreceive more significant flooding and property damage due to rapid\nrunoff.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Heavy showers and isolated thunderstorms will develop tonight and\ncontinue through Thursday as deep tropical moisture is drawn\nnorthward over the state. Training of heavy showers containing\nintense rain rates will be possible.",
                "instruction": "You should monitor later forecasts and be prepared to take action\nshould Flash Flood Warnings be issued.",
